mark/fio#1-test-environment-configuration","content":"Test instance type: Alibaba Cloud ECS i5.8xlarge, with 32-core CPU and 256 GB memory.","locale":"en"},"476":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio-15","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/fio#1-test-environment-configuration","content":"Network bandwidth: 80 Gbps, ensuring that data transmission has no network bottleneck.","locale":"en"},"477":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio-16","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/fio#1-test-environment-configuration","content":"Deployment architecture: 1 server independently deployed with `curvine-master` and `curvine-worker` services; 1 server deployed with the FUSE client to simulate business access.","locale":"en"},"478":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio-17","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/fio#1-test-environment-configuration","content":"Storage configuration: `curvine-worker` mounts 1 SSD disk. The upper limit of disk performance is 16 GB/s for reads and 28 GB/s for writes.","locale":"en"},"479":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio-18","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/fio#2-100g-large-file-performance-test","content":"For this large file test, `block_size` is uniformly set to 1G. The FIO tool is used for performance testing. FIO is a common I/O benchmark tool on Linux/Unix and can accurately simulate various storage read/write workloads. The test scenarios include write test, 256k sequential read, and 256k random read. The detailed test process and results are as follows:","locale":"en"},"480":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio-19","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/fio#21-write-test","content":"Test purpose: verify the sequential write performance of a 100G large file. A 256k block size is used, and kernel cache is bypassed with `direct=1` to ensure that the test results reflect the real storage write capability.","locale":"en"},"481":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio-20","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/fio#21-write-test","content":"Execution command:","locale":"en"},"482":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio-21","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/fio#22-256k-sequential-read-test","content":"Test purpose: verify the 256k sequential read performance of a 100G large file under different thread counts. The test duration is 60 seconds, kernel cache is bypassed, and the focus is on observing how bandwidth changes with the number of threads.","locale":"en"},"483":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio-22","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/fio#22-256k-sequential-read-test","content":"Execution command:","locale":"en"},"484":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio-23","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/fio#22-256k-sequential-read-test","content":"Test results, corresponding relationship between thread count and read speed:","locale":"en"},"485":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio-24","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/fio#22-256k-sequential-read-test","content":"| Thread Count | Read Speed (GiB/s) |\n| ------------ | ------------------ |\n| 1            | 2.1                |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"486":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio-25","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/fio#22-256k-sequential-read-test","content":"| Thread Count | Read Speed (GiB/s) |\n| ------------ | ------------------ |\n| 2            | 3.7                |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"487":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio-26","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/fio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/fio#22-256k-sequential-read-test","content":"| Thread Count | Read Speed (GiB/s) |\n| ------------ | ------------------ |\n| 4            | 6.1                |","locale":