                                                                                              |\n| ------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `worker_max_queued_tasks` | `0`     | Tasks a Worker holds at once (waiting plus running); beyond it new tasks get a retryable \"queue full\" answer. `0` means 2 × `worker_max_concurrent_tasks` |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"1323":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-404","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#job","content":"| Field                       | Default | Meaning                                                                                                     |\n| --------------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `worker_queue_full_timeout` | `30m`   | How long one submission may wait for a full Worker queue to drain before the dispatch gives up on that task |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"1324":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-405","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#job","content":"| Field                   | Default | Meaning                                                                                                              |\n| ----------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `load_parallel_streams` | `8`     | Parallel read streams per object for load and export tasks; mounts can override it with `load_task.parallel_streams` |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"1325":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-406","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#job","content":"| Field                       | Default | Meaning                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `load_min_bytes_per_stream` | `32MB`  | Minimum source bytes per stream: an object gets `len / load_min_bytes_per_stream` streams, capped by `load_parallel_streams`; mounts can override it with `load_task.min_bytes_per_stream` |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"1326":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-407","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#job","content":"| Field                 | Default           | Meaning                                                                                   |\n| --------------------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ufs_read_chunk_size` | `2097152` (2 MiB) | Range size of one UFS read request; mounts can override it with `opendal.read_chunk_size` |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"1327":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-408","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#job","content":"| Field                 | Default | Meaning                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ufs_read_concurrent` | `4`     | Range requests each stream keeps in flight; mounts can override it with `opendal.read_concurrent`. One object buffers about `load_parallel_streams × ufs_read_concurrent × ufs_read_chunk_size` (64 MiB by default) and a Worker up to `worker_max_concurrent_tasks` of those, so raise them with the Worker memory in mind |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"1328":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-409","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#transfer","content":"`[transfer]` is read by the standalone Transfer service and by clients that submit Load and Export work to it. A Transfer service also needs the normal `[client]` Master addresses. During a staged rollout, keep this section disabled in the Master and Worker configuration and enable it only in the Transfer and selected client configurations.","locale":"en"},"1329":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-410","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#transfer","content":"| Field     | Default | Meaning                                                                                                                              |\n| --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `enabled` | `false` | Enable Transfer routing in this process. On a client, `load` and `export` use Transfer; on a Transfer server, it starts the service. |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"1330":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-411","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#transfer","content":"| Field       | Default                                                 | Meaning                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `store_url` | empty; inferred as `sqlite://data/transfer/transfer.db` | State store URL. Schemes: `memory://`, `sqlite://`, `mysql://`, `postgres://`, `postgresql://`. Use one shared `mysql://` or `postgres://` URL for multiple instances. |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"1331":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-412","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#transfer","content":"| Field      | Default     | Meaning                                                            |\n| ---------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `hostname` | `localhost` | RPC and web bind hostname when explicit endpoints are not supplied |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"1332":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-413","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#transfer","content":"| Field      | Default | Meaning           |\n| ---------- | ------- | ----------------- |\n| `rpc_port` | `9010`  | Transfer RPC port |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"1333":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-414","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#transfer","content":"| Field      | Default | Meaning                      |\n| ---------- | ------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `web_port` | `9011`  | Health and metrics HTTP port |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"1334":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-415","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#transfer","content":"| Field       | Default                     | Meaning                                                                      |\n| ----------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `endpoints` | `[\"<hostname>:<rpc_port>\"]` | Client-facing Transfer RPC addresses; use a Service or load-balancer address |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"1335":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-416","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#transfer","content":"| Field         | Default | Meaning                                                          |\n| ------------- | -