55":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-15","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#start-from-a-release-package","content":"`CURVINE_MASTER_HOSTNAME=localhost` is suitable for single-node local use. In multi-node or containerized environments, set `CURVINE_MASTER_HOSTNAME`, `CURVINE_WORKER_HOSTNAME`, and `CURVINE_CLIENT_HOSTNAME` to addresses that other nodes and clients can actually reach.","locale":"en"},"1956":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-16","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#start-from-a-release-package","content":"By default, FUSE is mounted at `/curvine-fuse`.","locale":"en"},"1957":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-17","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#verify-the-cluster","content":"Use the native CLI to confirm that Master and Worker are reachable:","locale":"en"},"1958":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-18","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#verify-the-cluster","content":"Create a test directory and list it back:","locale":"en"},"1959":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-19","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#verify-the-cluster","content":"You can also validate the FUSE path directly:","locale":"en"},"1960":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-20","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#optional-compatibility-shell","content":"The release also includes `bin/dfs`, a compatibility wrapper for Hadoop-style `fs` commands:","locale":"en"},"1961":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-21","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#optional-compatibility-shell","content":"Use `cv` for the full Curvine-native command set. Use `dfs` only when you specifically need Hadoop shell style.","locale":"en"},"1962":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-22","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#web-ui","content":"The admin console is a standalone process, not part of the master. Start it when you need the UI:","locale":"en"},"1963":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-23","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#web-ui","content":"After startup, the main web endpoints are:","locale":"en"},"1964":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-24","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#web-ui","content":"Admin console (`curvine-web`): `http://<host>:9000` — overview, file browser, workers, monitoring","locale":"en"},"1965":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-25","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#web-ui","content":"Master metrics: `http://<host>:9010/metrics` — Prometheus text output only, no UI","locale":"en"},"1966":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-26","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#web-ui","content":"Worker: `http://<host>:9002`","locale":"en"},"1967":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-27","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#web-ui","content":"FUSE: `http://<host>:9003`","locale":"en"},"1968":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-28","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#about-benchmark-scripts","content":"The benchmark and stress-test scripts live in the source tree under `build/tests/`; they are not the primary entry point of a release-package quick start. For throughput and FIO testing, refer to the Benchmark and Contribute sections instead of using this page as a benchmark guide.","locale":"en"},"1969":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","type":"page","content":"System Requirements","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","locale":"en"},"1970":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements-0","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements#officially-supported-linux-distributions","content":"Officially Supported Linux Distributions","locale":"en"},"1971":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements-1","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","content":"This page summarizes the base requirements to build and run Curvine. For a full, step-by-step environment setup (including per-OS installation commands), see Environment Initialization.","locale":"en"},"1972":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements-2","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","content":"Rust 1.98 (pinned by `rust-toolchain.toml`; minimum accepted by `build/check-env.sh` is 1.86)","locale":"en"},"1973":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements-3","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","content":"Linux or macOS (Limited support on Windows)","locale":"en"},"1974":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements-4","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","content":"FUSE library (for file system functionality)","locale":"en"},"1975":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements-5","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements#officially-supported-linux-distributions","content":"| OS Distribution | Kernel Requirement | Tested Version | Dependencies |\n| --------------- | ------------------ | -------------- | ------------ |\n| **CentOS 7**    | ≥3.10.0            | 7.6            | fuse2-2.9.2  |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1976":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements-6","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements#officially-supported-linux-distributions","content":"| OS Distribution | Kernel Requirement | Tested Version | Dependencies |\n| --------------- | ------------------ | -------------- | ------------ |\n| **CentOS 8**    | ≥4.18.0            | 8.5            | fuse3-3.9.1  |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1977":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements-7","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements#officially-supported-linux-distributions","content":"| OS Distribution   | Kernel Requirement | Tested Version | Dependencies |\n| ----------------- | ------------------ | -------------- | ------------ |\n| **Rocky Linux 9** | ≥5.14.0            | 9.5            | fuse3-3.10.2 |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1978":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements-8","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements#officially-supported-linux-distributions","content":"| OS Distribution | Kernel Requirement | Tested Version | Dependencies |\n| --------------- | ------------------ | -------------- | ------------ |\n| **RHEL 9**      | ≥5.14.0            | 9.5            | fuse3-3.10.2 |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1979":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements-9","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/system-requirements#officially-supported-linux-distributions","content":"| OS Distribution | Kernel Requirement | Tested Version | Dependencies |\n| --------------- | ------------------ | -------------- | ------------ |\n| **Ubuntu 22**   | ≥5.15.0            | 22.4           | fuse3-3.10.5 |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1980":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","type":"page","content":"Technical Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Overview"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview/architecture","locale":"en"},"1981":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-0","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"Architecture Overview","locale":"en"},"1982":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-1","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-performance-design","content":"High-Performance Design","locale":"en"},"1983":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-2","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-availability-design","content":"High Availability Design","locale":"en"},"1984":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-3","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture","content":"This chapter provides an in-depth introduction to Curvine's technical architecture, detailing the functionality, interaction patterns, and design principles of each layer component to help you comprehensively understand how the Curvine system works.","locale":"en"},"1985":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-4","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"Curvine adopts a layered distributed architecture design that ensures clear component responsibilities with excellent scalability and high availability. The entire architecture is primarily divided into three layers: **control layer** (Master), **storage layer** (Workers), and **access layer** (clients: FUSE, SDK, CLI), which collaborate to complete data storage, processing, and management tasks.","locale":"en"},"1986":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-5","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"Curvine consists of three main server-side roles plus clients and UFS:","locale":"en"},"1987":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-6","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**Curvine Client**: Data read/write operations are implemented by the client, which calls Curvine server-side interfaces through RPC (metadata from Master, block data from Workers). The client supports multiple access methods:","locale":"en"},"1988":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**FUSE Mount**: POSIX-compatible mount via libfuse/3 (curvine-fuse)","locale":"en"},"1989":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**HDFS & SDK**: Java / Python / libsdk interfaces","locale":"en"},"1990":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**CSI Driver**: Kubernetes volume driver (curvine-csi)","locale":"en"},"1991":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**CLI (`cv`)**: Admin tools for fs ops, report, and cluster management","locale":"en"},"1992":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"Internally, the client layer is composed of:","locale":"en"},"1993":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**UnifiedFileSystem**: Provides unified namespace with CurvineFS + UFS fallback","locale":"en"},"1994":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-13","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**FsReader / FsWriter**: Parallel, buffered I/O with zero-copy optimization","locale":"en"},"1995":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-14","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**BlockClient Pool**: Manages block_reader / block_writer for local and remote access","locale":"en"},"1996":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-15","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**Mount & Meta Cache**: Caches mount info and inode metadata","locale":"en"},"1997":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-16","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**Master**: The core control node; responsible for metadata (directory tree, file inodes, block locations), Worker registration, block allocation, and UFS mount table. Master can run as multiple nodes forming a Raft group for high availability; only the Raft leader serves metadata writes.","locale":"en"},"1998":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-17","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"The Master cluster mainly includes:","locale":"en"},"1999":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-18","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**MasterServer**: RPC handling and routing","locale":"en"},"2000":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-19","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**MasterFilesystem**: File system operations (mkdir, create, rename, delete, li