le ensuring code safety and stability","locale":"en"},"2032":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-51","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-performance-design","content":"**High-Performance RPC Framework**: Curvine implements a custom RPC communication framework supporting efficient data transmission with asynchronous I/O and zero-copy implementation within the framework","locale":"en"},"2033":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-52","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-performance-design","content":"**Zero-Cost Abstractions**: Zero-cost abstraction design where core modules directly interface with underlying systems, avoiding unnecessary abstraction layers and improving system performance and resource utilization","locale":"en"},"2034":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-53","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-performance-design","content":"**Asynchronous I/O**: Asynchronous I/O design fully utilizes system resources, avoiding blocking waits and improving system concurrent processing capabilities","locale":"en"},"2035":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-54","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-performance-design","content":"**Zero-Copy**: Zero-copy design avoids data copying and memory allocation, reducing system memory usage and resource consumption","locale":"en"},"2036":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-55","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-availability-design","content":"Curvine adopts distributed architecture design with multi-replica mechanisms and failover mechanisms to ensure system high availability:","locale":"en"},"2037":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-56","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-availability-design","content":"**Raft Protocol**: Uses Raft protocol to implement distributed consistency, ensuring data consistency and reliability","locale":"en"},"2038":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-57","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-availability-design","content":"**Automatic Failover**: Automatic failover mechanism that switches to backup nodes when primary nodes fail, ensuring system high availability","locale":"en"},"2039":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-58","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-availability-design","content":"**Multi-Replica Mechanism**: Multi-replica mechanism ensures data redundancy backup, improving system reliability and fault tolerance","locale":"en"},"2040":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-59","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#high-availability-design","content":"**Snapshot Mechanism**: Lightweight snapshot mechanism for periodic data backup, improving system recovery speed and stability","locale":"en"},"2041":{"id":"/docs/Overview","page_id":"/docs/Overview","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Overview"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview","locale":"en"},"2042":{"id":"/docs/Overview/introduction","page_id":"/docs/Overview/introduction","type":"page","content":"Curvine Overview","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Overview"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview/introduction","locale":"en"},"2043":{"id":"/docs/Overview/introduction-0","page_id":"/docs/Overview/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview/introduction#core-features","content":"Core Features","locale":"en"},"2044":{"id":"/docs/Overview/introduction-1","page_id":"/docs/Overview/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Overview/introduction#use-cases","content":"Use Cases","locale":"en"