bject-operations","content":"| Operation               | HTTP request            |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `DeleteObjects` (batch) | `POST /{bucket}?delete` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2274":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-60","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multipart-upload","content":"| Operation               | HTTP request                   |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `CreateMultipartUpload` | `POST /{bucket}/{key}?uploads` |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"2275":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-61","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multipart-upload","content":"| Operation    | HTTP request                                       |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `UploadPart` | `PUT /{bucket}/{key}?partNumber={n}&uploadId={id}` |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"2276":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-62","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multipart-upload","content":"| Operation                 | HTTP request                         |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `CompleteMultipartUpload` | `POST /{bucket}/{key}?uploadId={id}` |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"2277":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-63","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multipart-upload","content":"`CopyObject` and `AbortMultipartUpload` are not implemented, and `ListObjectsV2` does not paginate. See Limitations.","locale":"en"},"2278":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-64","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#path-mapping","content":"The gateway maps S3 paths onto the Curvine namespace without an extra prefix:","locale":"en"},"2279":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-65","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#path-mapping","content":"| S3 path            | Curvine path |\n| ------------------ | ------------ |\n| Bucket `my-bucket` | `/my-bucket` |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"2280":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-66","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#path-mapping","content":"| S3 path                            | Curvine path                 |\n| ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Object `my-bucket/folder/file.txt` | `/my-bucket/folder/file.txt` |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"2281":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-67","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#path-mapping","content":"Buckets are regular Curvine directories, and objects are regular files. A bucket must exist before objects can be written to it, and it can also be browsed through FUSE, the CLI, or the SDK.","locale":"en"},"2282":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-68","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#1-start-the-gateway","content":"In a release package, start the gateway with the shipped script:","locale":"en"},"2283":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-69","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#1-start-the-gateway","content":"When building from source, `build/build.sh` produces the binary in the release\ndistribution (the default `--package all` includes it). To build only the\ngateway:","locale":"en"},"2284":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-70","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#1-start-the-gateway","content":"The binary is written to `target/release/curvine-s3-gateway`.","locale":"en"},"2285":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-71","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#2-configure-the-cluster-connection","content":"The gateway reuses the regular Curvine cluster configuration file. Add an `[s3_gateway]` section for gateway-specific settings; the `[client]`, `[master]`, and other sections are used to connect to the cluster:","locale":"en"},"2286":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-72","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#2-configure-the-cluster-connection","content":"See Configuration for every option.","locale":"en"},"2287":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-73","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#3-create-credentials","content":"The gateway has no built-in default credentials. Generate a key pair and store it in the credential store:","locale":"en"},"2288":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-74","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#3-create-credentials","content":"Or register an existing pair (the access key must be 16–32 characters and the secret key 16–64 characters):","locale":"en"},"2289":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-75","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#3-create-credentials","content":"Both commands use the credential store selected by the configuration file. See Credential Management.","locale":"en"},"2290":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-76","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#4-start-the-gateway","content":"The default listen address is `0.0.0.0:9900`. Override it and the region on the command line:","locale":"en"},"2291":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-77","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#4-start-the-gateway","content":"`--listen` and `--region` override the configuration file only when they are set to a value other than their built-in defaults (`0.0.0.0:9900` and `us-east-1`). Use the configuration file for those two values, or pass a different value explicitly.","locale":"en"},"2292":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-78","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#command-line-arguments","content":"| Argument | Description                        | Default                    |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `--conf` | Curvine cluster configuration file | `etc/curvine-cluster.toml` |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"2293":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-79","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#command-line-arguments","content":"| Argument   | Description                  | Default        |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `--listen` | Listen address (`host:port`) | `0.0.0.0:9900` |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"2294":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-80","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#command-line-arguments","content":"| Argument   | Description          | Default     |\n| ---------- | -------------------- | ----------- |\n| `--region` | S3 region identifier | `us-east-1` |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"2295":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-81","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#command-line-arguments","content":"| Argument             | Description                        | Default                   |\n| -------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `--credentials-path` | Override the credential store path | Value from `[s3_gateway]` |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"2296":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-82","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#command-line-arguments","content":"| Argument | Description                                                        | Default |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------- |\n| `serve`  | Optional subcommand; starting without a subcommand serves requests | —       |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"2297":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-83","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#command-line-arguments","content":"| Argument                                | Description                       | Default |\n| --------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `credential add\\|generate\\|list\\|stats` | Credential management subcommands | —       |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"2298":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-84","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter | Type   | Default          | Description             |\n| --------- | ------ | ---------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `listen`  | string | `\"0.0.0.0:9900\"` | Listen address and port |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2299":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-85","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter | Type   | Default       | Description          |\n| --------- | ------ | ------------- | -------------------- |\n| `region`  | string | `\"us-east-1\"` | S3 region identifier |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2300":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-86","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter      | Type   | Default               | Description                                                                          |\n| -------------- | ------ | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `put_temp_dir` | string | `\"/tmp/curvine-temp\"` | Temporary directory for PUT operations (regular and multipart) in local storage mode |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2301":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-87","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter                     | Type    | Default   | Description                                                         |\n| ----------------------------- | ------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `put_memory_buffer_threshold` | integer | `1048576` | Objects smaller than this (bytes) are buffered in memory during PUT |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2302":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-88","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter               | Type    | Default    | Description                                   |\n| ----------------------- | ------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `put_max_memory_buffer` | integer | `16777216` | Maximum in-memory buffer size for PUT (bytes) |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2303":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-89","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter           | Type  | Default | Description                                    |\n| ------------------- | ----- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `get_chunk_size_mb` | float | `1.0`   | Read/write chunk size for GET responses, in MB |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2304":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-90","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter                 | Type    | Default | Description                                                  |\n| ------------------------- | ------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `enable_distributed_auth` | boolean | `false` | Store credentials in Curvine instead of the local filesystem |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2305":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-91","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter          | Type   | Default   | Description           |\n| ------------------ | ------ | --------- | --------------------- |\n| `credentials_path` | string | See below | Credential store path |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2306":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-92","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter                     | Type    | Default | Description                                   |\n| ----------------------------- | ------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `cache_refresh_interval_secs` | integer | `30`    | Credential cache refresh interval, in seconds |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2307":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-93","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"`worker.enable_s3_gateway` (in the `[worker]` section) selects distributed multipart storage: upload parts are written under `/.s3temp` in Curvine instead of `put_temp_dir`, so any gateway instance can complete an upload. Setting it also switches the binary to the distributed credential store.","locale":"en"},"2308":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-94","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"**Credential store path:**","locale":"en"},"2309":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-95","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"Local mode (`enable_distributed_auth = false`): defaults to `~/.curvine/credentials.jsonl`","locale":"en"},"2310":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-96","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"Distributed mode (`enable_distributed_auth = true`): defaults to `/system/auth/credentials.jsonl`","locale":"en"},"2311":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-97","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"**Example configuration:**","locale":"en"},"2312":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-98","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#credential-management","content":"Credentials are stored in JSONL format, one entry per line:","locale":"en"},"2313":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-99","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#environment-variables","content":"| Variable                                    | Description |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` or `CURVINE_ACCESS_KEY` | Access key  |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2314":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-100","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#environment-variables","content":"| Variable                                        | Description |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` or `CURVINE_SECRET_KEY` | Secret key  |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2315":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-101","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#environment-variables","content":"| Variable   | Description                                                               |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `RUST_LOG` | Log level (for example `info`, `debug`, `curvine_s3_gateway::auth=debug`) |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2316":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-102","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#environment-variables","content":"The gateway imports environment credentials only when the configured credential store is empty; the imported pair is written to the local credential store. If neither a stored credential nor an environment pair is available, the gateway starts with an empty store and rejects every request.","locale":"en"},"2317":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-103","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#commands","content":"`credential list --show-secrets` and `credential generate` print secret keys to the terminal. Treat that output as sensitive and avoid shell history or shared logs.","locale":"en"},"2318":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-104","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#usage-examples","content":"The examples below use `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`. Export the pair you created in Getting Started first:","locale":"en"},"2319":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-105","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#range-requests","content":"Range responses use status `206` and include a `Content-Range` header. Signed requests are easiest to produce through an S3 SDK or the AWS CLI.","locale":"en"},"2320":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-106","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multipart-upload-1","content":"`AbortMultipartUpload` is not routed yet, so an abandoned upload leaves its parts in the temporary storage directory. Remove them manually.","locale":"en"},"2321":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-107","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#single-instance","content":"Run the binary under your process manager (systemd, supervisor, Kubernetes). No start/stop script is shipped yet:","locale":"en"},"2322":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-108","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multiple-instances","content":"The gateway is stateless apart from temporary multipart data and credentials, so it can run behind a load balancer:","locale":"en"},"2323":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-109","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multiple-instances","content":"For more than one gateway instance, enable distributed multipart storage and distributed credentials so that any instance can complete an upload:","locale":"en"},"2324":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-110","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multiple-instances","content":"Without distributed storage, upload parts stay in the local `put_temp_dir` of the instance that received them; a `CompleteMultipartUpload` routed to a different instance cannot find them. Alternatively, configure session affinity on the load balancer.","locale":"en"},"2325":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-111","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#monitoring-and-logging","content":"The gateway logs through `tracing` to stdout. Adjust the level with `RUST_LOG`:","locale":"en"},"2326":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-112","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#monitoring-and-logging","content":"Logs cover request handling, authentication failures, multipart operations, and filesystem errors. There is no metrics endpoint yet; use the `/healthz` endpoint for liveness checks.","locale":"en"},"2327":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-113","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#limitations","content":"`CopyObject` is not implemented; clients must download and re-upload.","locale":"en"},"2328":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-114","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#limitations","content":"`AbortMultipartUpload` is not implemented; abandoned uploads leave temporary parts behind.","locale":"en"},"2329":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-115","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#limitations","content":"`ListObjectsV2` returns a single page: `continuation-token` and `max-keys` are ignored, and `is-truncated` is always `false`.","locale":"en"},"2330":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-116","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#limitations","content":"Conditional request headers (`If-Match`, `If-None-Match`) are accepted but not evaluated.","locale":"en"},"2331":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-117","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#limitations","content":"When Curvine trash is enabled, `DeleteObject` and `DeleteBucket` move data into the recycle bin instead of removing it permanently.","locale":"en"},"2332":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-118","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#port-already-in-use","content":"Change the listen address in `[s3_gateway]` or pass a different `--listen` value:","locale":"en"},"2333":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-119","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#configuration-file-errors","content":"If the configuration file cannot be loaded, the gateway prints a warning and continues with defaults. Verify the path and TOML syntax:","locale":"en"},"2334":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-120","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#bucket-not-found","content":"Create the bucket before uploading (`aws s3 mb`), because the gateway does not create buckets implicitly.","locale":"en"},"2335":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-121","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#performance-tuning","content":"For large-object workloads, increase `get_chunk_size_mb` and make sure `put_temp_dir` is on fast local storage. When `worker.enable_s3_gateway = true`, multipart parts are written directly to Curvine and `put_temp_dir` is not used for them.","locale":"en"},"2336":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"page","content":"SDK Access","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals","Access"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","locale":"en"},"2337":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-0","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"Overview","locale":"en"},"2338":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-1","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#rust-sdk","content":"Rust SDK","locale":"en"},"2339":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-2","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#java-sdk","content":"Java SDK","locale":"en"},"2340":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-3","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#hadoop-filesystem","content":"Hadoop FileSystem","locale":"en"},"2341":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-4","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#java-api","content":"Java API","locale":"en"},"2342":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-5","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#python-sdk","content":"Python SDK","locale":"en"},"2343":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-6","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#common-configuration","content":"Common Configuration","locale":"en"},"2344":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-7","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","content":"Curvine provides multi-language SDKs so applications can access the Curvine filesystem via RPC (metadata from Master, block data from Workers) without using FUSE.","locale":"en"},"2345":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-8","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"| SDK      | Crate / Package                     | Use Case                                   |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Rust** | `curvine-client` / `curvine-libsdk` | Native Rust applications, high performance |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2346":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-9","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"| SDK      | Crate / Package                                                                                      | Use Case                                      |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| **Java** | `io.curvine.CurvineFileSystem` (Hadoop `FileSystem`, scheme `cv://`), plus `curvine-libsdk` Java SDK | Hadoop/Spark/Flink and other JVM applications |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2347":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-10","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"| SDK        | Crate / Package                                                         | Use Case                                |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| **Python** | `curvinefs` — `CurvineClient` (native) and `CurvineFileSystem` (fsspec) | ML/data pipelines, pandas/dask, scripts |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2348":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-11","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"All SDKs require a running Curvine cluster (Master and Workers) and correct client configuration (e.g. `master_addrs` in `curvine-cluster.toml` or equivalent).","locale":"en"},"2349":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-12","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#rust-sdk","content":"Use the `curvine-client` crate (or the Rust API exposed by `curvine-libsdk`) to create files, read/write data, and list directories programmatically. Configuration is typically loaded from `curvine-cluster.toml` or via environment variables.","locale":"en"},"2350":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-13","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#rust-sdk","content":"For build and usage, see the Development Guide and the Curvine source repository (e.g. `curvine-client`, `curvine-libsdk`, and integration tests under `curvine-tests`).","locale":"en"},"2351":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-14","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#hadoop-filesystem","content":"The Hadoop path uses the URI scheme **`cv://`** (not `fs.cv://`) and\n`io.curvine.CurvineFileSystem`, so `FileSystem.get(URI.create(\"cv://default/path\"), conf)`\nreturns a Curvine client.","locale":"en"},"2352":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-15","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#hadoop-filesystem","content":"All `filesystemConf` fields are read as `fs.cv.<field>`, where `<field>` is the\nfield name on `io.curvine.FilesystemConf` — `fs.cv.master_addrs`, not\n`fs.cv.default.master_addrs`. Anything you can set in `curvine-cluster.toml`\nunder `[client]` can be overridden this way, and `-D` system properties win\nover the configuration file.","locale":"en"},"2353":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-16","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#hadoop-filesystem","content":"Optional keys:","locale":"en"},"2354":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-17","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#hadoop-filesystem","content":"| Key                      | Default | Meaning                                        |\n| ------------------------ | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `fs.cv.transfer.enabled` | `false` | Route load/export through the Transfer service |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2355":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-18","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#hadoop-filesystem","content":"| Key                        | Default | Meaning                |\n| -------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------- |\n| `fs.cv.transfer.endpoints` | —       | Transfer RPC endpoints |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2356":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-19","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#hadoop-filesystem","content":"| Key                   | Default | Meaning                                  |\n| --------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `fs.cv.proxy.enabled` | `true`  | Enable the ZooKeeper-backed proxy switch |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2357":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-20","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#hadoop-filesystem","content":"| Key                     | Default | Meaning                           |\n| ----------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `fs.cv.proxy.zk.server` | empty   | ZooKeeper servers for that switch |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2358":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-21","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#hadoop-filesystem","content":"| Key                   | Default                  | Meaning                          |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------ | -------------------------------- |\n| `fs.cv.proxy.zk.path` | `/curvine/proxy_enabled` | ZooKeeper znode holding the flag |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2359":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-22","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#hadoop-filesystem","content":"| Key                   | Default | Meaning                      |\n| --------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `fs.cv.proxy.timeout` | `60s`   | Timeout for the proxy lookup |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2360":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-23","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#hadoop-filesystem","content":"| Key                        | Default   | Meaning                               |\n| -------------------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `fs.cv.proxy.cluster.name` | `default` | Cluster name used by the proxy lookup |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2361":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-24","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#hadoop-filesystem","content":"For Spark, set the same keys with the `spark.hadoop.` prefix, e.g.\n`--conf spark.hadoop.fs.cv.master_addrs=master1:8995`.","locale":"en"},"2362":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-25","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#java-api","content":"`io.curvine.CurvineFileSystem` also works directly (open/create/append/stat/…),\nand `CurvineLoadClient` / `CurvineTransferClient` / `CurvineMountClient` cover\nload, transfer, and mount operations from JVM code without shelling out.","locale":"en"},"2363":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-26","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#java-api","content":"Compatible with Hadoop, Spark, Flink, and other JVM-based frameworks that support custom FileSystem implementations.","locale":"en"},"2364":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-27","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#python-sdk","content":"`curvinefs` ships two entry points:","locale":"en"},"2365":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-28","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#python-sdk","content":"**`CurvineClient`** — native bindings, explicit config, chunks you control:","locale":"en"},"2366":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-29","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#python-sdk","content":"**`CurvineFileSystem`** — an fsspec implementation, registered as the\n