tions/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"S3 (`s3://`, `s3a://`)","locale":"en"},"2973":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-23","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#oss-oss","content":"OSS (`oss://`)","locale":"en"},"2974":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-24","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"HDFS (`hdfs://`)","locale":"en"},"2975":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-25","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#webhdfs-webhdfs","content":"WebHDFS (`webhdfs://`)","locale":"en"},"2976":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-26","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","content":"This section is based on the current repository source in `curvine-cli`, `build/cv`, and `build/bin/dfs`. Curvine currently exposes three CLI entry styles:","locale":"en"},"2977":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-27","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","content":"**Native Rust CLI `cv`**: the recommended entry point, with the full command tree from `curvine-cli`.","locale":"en"},"2978":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-28","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","content":"**Compatibility wrapper `dfs`**: bundled in the distribution; `fs` / `report` go through Java `CurvineShell` and keep Hadoop `FsShell` style.","locale":"en"},"2979":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-29","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","content":"**POSIX / FUSE**: after mounting with FUSE, use standard Linux commands directly on the mount point.","locale"