ale":"en"},"2991":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-41","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"**Usage:** `cv report [json|all|capacity|used|available]`","locale":"en"},"2992":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-42","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"| Command     | Description                                                                               |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv report` | Default summary, including active master, capacity, inode/block counts, and worker lists. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2993":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-43","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"| Command          | Description                         |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `cv report json` | Emit the full `MasterInfo` as JSON. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2994":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-44","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"| Command                              | Description                                            |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `cv report all --show-workers false` | Text summary, with optional worker detail suppression. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2995":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-45","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"| Command                               | Description                                                      |\n| ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv report capacity [WORKER_ADDRESS]` | Show cluster-wide capacity, or detailed capacity for one worker. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2996":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-46","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"| Command          | Description                              |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `cv report used` | Show used capacity for each live worker. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2997":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-47","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"| Command               | Description                                   |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv report available` | Show available capacity for each live worker. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2998":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-48","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2999":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-49","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#1-report-cluster-status","content":"In the current implementation, `cv report capacity <WORKER_ADDRESS>` matches by worker IP address, not by `hostname:port`.","locale":"en"},"3000":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-50","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"**Usage:** `cv node [OPTIONS] [-- <NODES>...]`","locale":"en"},"3001":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-51","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"| Option       | Description                 |\n| ------------ | --------------------------- |\n| `-l, --list` | List live and lost workers. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3002":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-52","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"| Option       | Description                                                |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--versions` | Show release-version distribution across all live workers. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3003":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-53","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"| Option                          | Description                                       |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--add-decommission <NODES>...` | Add one or more workers to the decommission list. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3004":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-54","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"| Option                             | Description                                            |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--remove-decommission <NODES>...` | Remove one or more workers from the decommission list. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3005":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-55","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"`<NODES>` supports two forms:","locale":"en"},"3006":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-56","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"Space-separated arguments: `host1:8997 host2:8997`","locale":"en"},"3007":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-57","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"A single comma-separated argument: `host1:8997,host2:8997`","locale":"en"},"3008":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-58","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"3009":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-59","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"`cv node --versions` prints the release-version distribution across live\nworkers, preferring the structured `component_info.release_version` reported on\nheartbeat and falling back to the legacy `software_version` string:","locale":"en"},"3010":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-60","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"See Version Management and Compatibility for the\nmeaning of these versions and how the master evaluates mixed-version peers.","locale":"en"},"3011":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-61","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#2-node-worker-management","content":"The current implementation strips `hostname:port` down to `hostname` before calling the decommission API. The port is mainly for readability and consistent input format.","locale":"en"},"3012":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-62","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"**Usage:** `cv fs [OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [ARGS]`","locale":"en"},"3013":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-63","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"`fs` adds one command-level global switch:","locale":"en"},"3014":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-64","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Option         | Description                                                                             |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--cache-only` | Query / operate only on data already cached in Curvine, disabling the unified UFS view. |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"3015":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-65","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"The current source exposes these `fs` subcommands:","locale":"en"},"3016":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-66","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command           | Description                         |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `cv fs ls [PATH]` | List a directory, default path `/`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3017":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-67","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command                              | Description         |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------- |\n| `cv fs mkdir <PATH> [-p\\|--parents]` | Create a directory. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3018":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-68","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command                                                   | Description                                                           |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv fs put <LOCAL_PATH> <REMOTE_PATH> [-n\\|--no-clobber]` | Upload a local file into Curvine; `-n` keeps an existing destination. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3019":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-69","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command                         | Description                            |\n| ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `cv fs get <PATH> <LOCAL_PATH>` | Download a Curvine file to local disk. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3020":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-70","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command                                      | Description                                   |\n| -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv fs cat <PATH> [--offset N] [--length N]` | Print file contents, optionally a byte range. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3021":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-71","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command                             | Description                                      |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `cv fs tail <PATH> [-n\\|--bytes N]` | Print the last bytes of a file, 1024 by default. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3022":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-72","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command              | Description                                |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `cv fs touch <PATH>` | Create an empty file or update timestamps. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3023":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-73","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command                                                                    | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv fs rm <PATH> [-r\\|--recursive] [--skip-trash] [--async] [-f\\|--force]` | Remove a file or directory. `--skip-trash` deletes permanently, bypassing the recycle bin if it is enabled; `--async` returns immediately and lets the Master reclaim the entry in the background (Curvine paths only); `-f` ignores a path that does not exist. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3024":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-74","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command          | Description                          |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `cv fs trash ls` | List the entries in the recycle bin. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3025":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-75","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command                                                         | Description                                                                                             |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv fs trash restore <TRASH_PATH> [--dst <PATH>] [--overwrite]` | Restore a recycle-bin entry such as `/.Trash/1700000000000-42` to its original location, or to `--dst`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3026":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-76","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command                      | Description                                                                                                                          |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `cv fs trash empty [--wait]` | Permanently delete every entry in the recycle bin; `--wait` waits until the Master has reclaimed them and prints the reclaimed size. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3027":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-77","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command                      | Description                                                |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv fs stat <PATH> [--json]` | Show file or directory status; `--json` prints it as JSON. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3028":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-78","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command              | Description                             |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `cv fs count <PATH>` | Count files / directories under a path. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3029":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-79","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command                          | Description     |\n| -------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| `cv fs mv <SRC_PATH> <DST_PATH>` | Move or rename. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3030":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-80","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Command                     | Description                 |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `cv fs du <PATH> [-h] [-v]` | Show directory space usage. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3031":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-81","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"