ported schemes |","locale":"en","table":"table-7"},"3070":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-120","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Value      | Description                            | Typical protocols |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `oss-hdfs` | Use JindoSDK / OSS-HDFS path handling. | `oss://`          |","locale":"en","table":"table-7"},"3071":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-121","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Value     | Description                 | Typical protocols                                                                 |\n| --------- | --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `opendal` | Use OpenDAL-based backends. | `s3://`, `oss://`, `hdfs://`, `webhdfs://`, `cos://`, `gcs://`, `azblob://`, etc. |","locale":"en","table":"table-7"},"3072":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-122","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"There are also a few implementation details worth calling out:","locale":"en"},"3073":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-123","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"For `s3://...` paths, if `s3.bucket_name` is not provided explicitly, the CLI auto-fills it from the URI.","locale":"en"},"3074":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-124","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"For `hdfs://...` paths, if `hdfs.namenode` / `hdfs.root` are not provided explicitly, the CLI derives them from the URI.","locale":"en"},"3075":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-125","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"If the config contains `hdfs.kerberos.*` keys but neither `hdfs.kerberos.ccache` nor the `KRB5CCNAME` environment variable is present, the CLI prints a Kerberos ticket-cache warning.","locale":"en"},"3076":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-126","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`validate_path_and_configs` currently applies extra path validation only to S3 paths; other schemes mostly rely on later provider initialization and connectivity checks.","locale":"en"},"3077":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-127","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"3078":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-128","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"For detailed parameter lists of each UFS type (S3, OSS, HDFS, WebHDFS), see Appendix: UFS Mount Parameters at the end.","locale":"en"},"3079":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-129","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`--check-path-consist=true` is enabled by default. That means a path such as `s3://bucket/datasets` is normally expected to mount to `/bucket/datasets`. If you really need a different mapping, pass `--check-path-consist=false` explicitly.","locale":"en"},"3080":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-130","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"In the current source, the first creation of an `fs_mode` mount automatically triggers a `resync`. Manual `cv mount resync ...` only works for `fs_mode` mount points.","locale":"en"},"3081":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-131","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#5-umount-remove-a-mount","content":"**Usage:** `cv umount <CURVINE_PATH>`","locale":"en"},"3082":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-132","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#5-umount-remove-a-mount","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"3083":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-133","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"**Usage:** `cv load [OPTIONS] <SOURCE_PATH> [TARGET_PATH]`","locale":"en"},"3084":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-134","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                               |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `<SOURCE_PATH>`   | UFS source URI or a Curvine path below an existing mount. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"3085":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-135","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                                                           |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `[TARGET_PATH]`   | Optional Curvine destination. A mounted source path derives its target automatically. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"3086":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-136","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                    |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `-w, --watch`     | Watch job status immediately after submission. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"3087":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-137","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                   |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `--no-overwrite`  | Fail instead of replacing an existing target. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"3088":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-138","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"3089":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-139","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"With Transfer enabled, `load` submits a Transfer job. Otherwise it uses the\nlegacy Master job path. The command prints a job ID and target path in either\nmode.","locale":"en"},"3090":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-140","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#transfer-routing","content":"The command line does not change when standalone Transfer is enabled:","locale":"en"},"3091":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-141","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#transfer-routing","content":"| Client configuration         | `cv load` / `cv export` route                       |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `[transfer] enabled = false` | Legacy Master Load API, for backward compatibility. |","locale":"en","table":"table-9"},"3092":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-142","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#transfer-routing","content":"| Client configuration        | `cv load` / `cv export` route                       |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `[transfer] enabled = true` | Transfer service RPC, selected directly by the CLI. |","locale":"en","table":"table-9"},"3093":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-143","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#transfer-routing","content":"The Transfer service and the client must both be configured for Transfer. Master\nand Worker configuration does not change for a client-side rollout. A client\nwith `transfer.enabled = false` continues to submit through the legacy Master\nAPI.","locale":"en"},"3094":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-144","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"**Usage:** `cv export [OPTIONS] <PATH>`","locale":"en"},"3095":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-145","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"`<PATH>` must be a Curvine path below a mount. Curvine infers the UFS target\nfrom that mount.","locale":"en"},"3096":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-146","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                    |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `<PATH>`          | Curvine source path to export. |","locale":"en","table":"table-10"},"3097":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-147","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                    |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `-w, --watch`     | Watch job status immediately after submission. |","locale":"en","table":"table-10"},"3098":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-148","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                              |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `--no-overwrite`  | Fail when the UFS target already exists. |","locale":"en","table":"table-10"},"3099":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-149","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"3100":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-150","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"**Usage:** `cv load-status [OPTIONS] <JOB_ID>`","locale":"en"},"3101":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-151","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"| Option / Argument | Description          |\n| ----------------- | -------------------- |\n| `<JOB_ID>`        | Load job identifier. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"3102":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-152","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"| Option / Argument | Description     |\n| ----------------- | --------------- |\n| `-v, --verbose`   | Verbose output. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"3103":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-153","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"| Option / Argument        | Description                                                                 |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `-w, --watch <INTERVAL>` | Poll interval, default `5s`. Supports formats such as `1s`, `1m`, and `1h`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"3104":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-154","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                                        |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--conf <PATH>`   | Optional one-command config override; normal use does not need it. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"3105":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-155","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"3106":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-156","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"In the current implementation, `load-status` enters watch mode by default with a `5s` refresh interval. The source does not currently expose a dedicated one-shot status-only switch.","locale":"en"},"3107":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-157","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#9-cancel-load-cancel-a-load-job","content":"**Usage:** `cv cancel-load [OPTIONS] <JOB_ID>`","locale":"en"},"3108":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-158","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#9-cancel-load-cancel-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description               |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `<JOB_ID>`        | Job identifier to cancel. |","locale":"en","table":"table-12"},"3109":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-159","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#9-cancel-load-cancel-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                                        |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--conf <PATH>`   | Optional one-command config override; normal use does not need it. |","locale":"en","table":"table-12"},"3110":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-160","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#9-cancel-load-cancel-a-load-job","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"3111":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-161","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-load-list-list-recent-load-and-export-jobs","content":"**Usage:** `cv load-list [OPTIONS]`","locale":"en"},"3112":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-162","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-load-list-list-recent-load-and-export-jobs","content":"| Option            | Description                                                     |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--path <PREFIX>` | Match jobs whose source or target path starts with this prefix. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"3113":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-163","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-load-list-list-recent-load-and-export-jobs","content":"| Option              | Description                                        |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--mount <CV_PATH>` | Match `fs_mode` jobs under one Curvine mount path. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"3114":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-164","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-load-list-list-recent-load-and-export-jobs","content":"| Option            | Description                                                               |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--state <STATE>` | Filter by state: `pending`, `loading`, `completed`, `failed`, `canceled`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"3115":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-165","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-load-list-list-recent-load-and-export-jobs","content":"| Option           | Description                     |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `--running-only` | Only show pending/loading jobs. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"3116":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-166","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-load-list-list-recent-load-and-export-jobs","content":"| Option          | Description                                                     |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--failed-only` | Only failed jobs; with `-v`, only failed task rows are printed. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"3117":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-167","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-load-list-list-recent-load-and-export-jobs","content":"| Option        | Description                           |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `--limit <N>` | Maximum jobs returned (default `50`). |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"3118":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-168","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-load-list-list-recent-load-and-export-jobs","content":"| Option         | Description                                                   |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--offset <N>` | Skip N jobs, most recent first, for pagination (default `0`). |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"3119":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-169","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-load-list-list-recent-load-and-export-jobs","content":"| Option          | Description                             |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `-v, --verbose` | Include task-level detail for each job. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"3120":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-170","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-load-list-list-recent-load-and-export-jobs","content":"| Option                      | Description                                              |\n| --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--include-finished <BOOL>` | Include completed/failed/canceled jobs (default `true`). |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"3121":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-171","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"`cv transfer` is available only when `[transfer] enabled = true`. It is the\noperations command for listing, inspecting, retrying, and paging Transfer jobs;\nnormal submission remains `cv load` or `cv export`.","locale":"en"},"3122":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-172","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"It requires a reachable Transfer endpoint in the client configuration. See\nTransfer Service for deployment.","locale":"en"},"3123":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-173","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command            | Description                                                                            |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer list` | List jobs. Filter with `--kind load\\|export`, `--state`, `--tenant`, or `--submitter`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"3124":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-174","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command                       | Description                                                                       |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer status <JOB_ID>` | Show one job. Add `--verbose` for task detail or `--watch --interval 1s` to poll. |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"3125":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-175","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command                      | Description                   |\n| ---------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer tasks <JOB_ID>` | Show a task page for one job. |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"3126":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-176","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command                       | Description            |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `cv transfer cancel <JOB_ID>` | Cancel a Transfer job. |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"3127":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-177","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command                      | Description                                                         |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer retry <JOB_ID>` | Retry a failed, canceled, or partially successful job as a new job. |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"3128":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-178","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command               | Description               |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer tenants` | Summarize jobs by tenant. |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"3129":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-179","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"3130":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-180","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"`load-status` and `cancel-load` remain compatible shortcuts. With Transfer\nenabled, they call Transfer; with Transfer disabled, they call the legacy\nMaster implementation.","locale":"en"},"3131":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-181","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#12-version-show-version","content":"**Usage:** `cv version`","locale":"en"},"3132":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-182","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#12-version-show-version","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"3133":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-183","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#12-version-show-version","content":"The current implementation prints `curvine-cli <version>` together with commit / branch information.","locale":"en"},"3134":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-184","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#12-version-show-version","content":"Every binary also accepts the global `--version-json` flag to print its full\nstructured version (component, release version, git provenance, protocol\nversion, capabilities) as JSON — see\nVersion Management and Compatibility:","locale":"en"},"3135":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-185","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#13-bench-built-in-benchmark","content":"**Usage:** `cv bench [OPTIONS]` and `cv bench prefill [OPTIONS]`","locale":"en"},"3136":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-186","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#13-bench-built-in-benchmark","content":"`bench` runs metadata and throughput suites against a `cv://` path (client mode)\nor `file://` path (FUSE mode). `cv bench prefill` creates a reusable working set\nfor mixed workloads. Common options include `--path`, `--profile basic|deep`,\n`--mode auto|client|fuse`, `-p/--threads`, `--workload`, `--block-size`,\n`--big-file-size`, and `--big-file-count`. Run `cv bench --help` for the full\noption list.","locale":"en"},"3137":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-187","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#14-fsck-block-replica-health","content":"**Usage:** `cv fsck <PATH> [OPTIONS]`","locale":"en"},"3138":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-188","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#14-fsck-block-replica-health","content":"| Option   | Description                   |\n| -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `<PATH>` | File or directory to inspect. |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"3139":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-189","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#14-fsck-block-replica-health","content":"| Option     | Description                                          |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--detail` | Show per-file and per-block details for directories. |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"3140":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-190","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#14-fsck-block-replica-health","content":"| Option                 | Description                                                        |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--list-page-size <N>` | Directory entries per listing RPC (default `256`, range `1-4096`). |","locale":"en","table":"table-15"},"3141":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-191","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#14-fsck-block-replica-health","content":"`fsck` compares the replicas recorded for each block with the replicas currently\navailable and reports under-replicated blocks and read errors. A warning line is\nprinted when the scan finds problems.","locale":"en"},"3142":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-192","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#15-admin-config-inspect-and-override-master-runtime-config","content":"**Usage:** `cv admin config <set|get|reset> ...`","locale":"en"},"3143":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-193","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#15-admin-config-inspect-and-override-master-runtime-config","content":"Runtime overrides apply to the running Master without editing the config file,\nand they are **not persistent**: a Master restart restores the file-backed\nvalues.","locale":"en"},"3144":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-194","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#15-admin-config-inspect-and-override-master-runtime-config","content":"| Command               | Description                                                                                  |\n| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv admin config get` | List every registered runtime-config key with its file value, override, and effective value. |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"3145":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-195","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#15-admin-config-inspect-and-override-master-runtime-config","content":"| Command                     | Description   |\n| --------------------------- | ------------- |\n| `cv admin config get <KEY>` | Show one key. |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"3146":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-196","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#15-admin-config-inspect-and-override-master-runtime-config","content":"| Command                             | Description                                                           |\n| ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv admin config set <KEY> <VALUE>` | Set an in-memory override and print the previous and effective value. |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"3147":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-197","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#15-admin-config-inspect-and-override-master-runtime-config","content":"| Command                       | Description                                               |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv admin config reset <KEY>` | Drop the override and fall back to the config-file value. |","locale":"en","table":"table-16"},"3148":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-198","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#15-admin-config-inspect-and-override-master-runtime-config","content":"In the current release the Master registers **no** runtime-adjustable keys\n(`build_master_runtime_registry` returns an empty registry). `cv admin config\nget` therefore prints `(no runtime config entries)`, and `set` / `reset` return\n`unsupported runtime configuration ...; writable: []`. The command surface is in\nplace for keys that will be registered later; use the config file plus a\nrestart for any change you need today.","locale":"en"},"3149":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-199","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#16-snapshot-create-a-master-metadata-snapshot","content":"**Usage:** `cv snapshot create [--force]`","locale":"en"},"3150":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-200","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#16-snapshot-create-a-master-metadata-snapshot","content":"Asks the active Master to create a metadata snapshot now, and prints the snapshot directory and how long the checkpoint took. Journal truncation and checkpoint retention are applied asynchronously.","locale":"en"},"3151":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-201","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#16-snapshot-create-a-master-metadata-snapshot","content":"A request within `journal.snapshot_min_interval` of the previous snapshot is rejected. `--force` runs the checkpoint anyway, stalling metadata writes while it runs.","locale":"en"},"3152":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-202","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#16-snapshot-create-a-master-metadata-snapshot","content":"The checkpoint runs on the Master and cannot be cancelled. On a large namespace it can take longer than `client.rpc_timeout_ms` (120s by default) even though it succeeds, and the retry then reports `a leader snapshot is already in progress`. Raise `client.rpc_timeout_ms` in the file passed with `--conf` first.","locale":"en"},"3153":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-203","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#17-completion-shell-completion-script","content":"**Usage:** `cv completion <SHELL>`","locale":"en"},"3154":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-204","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#17-completion-shell-completion-script","content":"Prints a completion script for `bash`, `zsh`, `fish`, `powershell` or `elvish`. For example, to enable completion in the current bash session:","locale":"en"},"3155":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-205","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"`bin/dfs` in the distribution is a compatibility wrapper:","locale":"en"},"3156":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-206","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"When the first subcommand is `fs` or `report`, it calls Java `io.curvine.CurvineShell`.","locale":"en"},"3157":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-207","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"`dfs fs` keeps Hadoop `FsShell` syntax, so subcommands look like `-ls`, `-mkdir`, `-rm -r` with single-dash command names.","locale":"en"},"3158":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-208","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"Other subcommands are eventually forwarded to the Rust `curvine-cli`, but for normal operations `cv` is still the recommended entry point.","locale":"en"},"3159":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-209","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"3160":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-210","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"`dfs report info` is the Java-compat text-summary variant; conceptually it is close to `cv report all`, but the command name is different.","locale":"en"},"3161":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-211","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"Use `dfs` when you need Hadoop shell compatibility or rely on Hadoop configuration files such as `core-site.xml` / `hdfs-site.xml`. Use `cv` when you want the full Curvine-native command set from current source.","locale":"en"},"3162":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-212","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Curvine also exposes a FUSE file system interface. After mounting it, for example via `bin/curvine-fuse.sh start`, you can operate on the mount point with normal Linux tools:","locale":"en"},"3163":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-213","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Typical categories:","locale":"en"},"3164":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-214","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Basic file operations: `ls`, `cp`, `mv`, `rm`, `mkdir`","locale":"en"},"3165":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-215","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Content inspection: `cat`, `grep`, `sed`","locale":"en"},"3166":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-216","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"File system information: `df -h`, `du -sh`, `stat`","locale":"en"},"3167":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-217","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Permissions: `chmod`, `chown`","locale":"en"},"3168":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-218","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"If your goal is POSIX compatibility with existing tools, prefer FUSE. If you need Curvine-native mount, load, or node-management features, use `cv`.","locale":"en"},"3169":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-219","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#appendix-ufs-mount-parameters","content":"The following are common parameters passed through `--config key=value` when using `cv mount`. `Required` means it normally must be provided; `Optional` means it can be omitted if a default exists or if the CLI can infer it from the mount URI.","locale":"en"},"3170":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-220","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"Used with `--provider opendal` or auto-selection.","locale":"en"},"3171":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-221","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter         | Required/Optional | Description                                                       |\n| ----------------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3.endpoint_url` | Required          | S3 service endpoint URL; must start with `http://` or `https://`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-17"},"3172":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-222","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter               | Required/Optional | Description    |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- | -------------- |\n| `s3.credentials.access` | Required          | Access Key ID. |","locale":"en","table":"table-17"},"3173":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-223","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter               | Required/Optional | Description        |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------ |\n| `s3.credentials.secret` | Required          | Secret Access Key. |","locale":"en","table":"table-17"},"3174":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-224","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter        | Required/Optional | Description  |\n| ---------------- | ----------------- | ------------ |\n| `s3.region_name` | Optional          | Region name. |","locale":"en","table":"table-17"},"3175":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-225","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter       | Required/Optional | Description                                                                       |\n| --------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3.path_style` | Optional          | Whether to use path-style access, commonly needed for MinIO-compatible endpoints. |","locale":"en","table":"table-17"},"3176":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-226","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#oss-oss","content":"For Alibaba Cloud OSS / OSS-HDFS style access.","locale":"en"},"3177":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-227","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#oss-oss","content":"| Parameter      | Required/Optional | Description           |\n| -------------- | ----------------- | --------------------- |\n| `oss.endpoint` | Required          | OSS endpoint address. |","locale":"en","table":"table-18"},"3178":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-228","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#oss-oss","content":"| Parameter         | Required/Optional | Description                 |\n| ----------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `oss.accessKeyId` | Required          | Alibaba Cloud AccessKey ID. |","locale":"en","table":"table-18"},"3179":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-229","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#oss-oss","content":"| Parameter             | Required/Optional | Description                     |\n| --------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `oss.accessKeySecret` | Required          | Alibaba Cloud AccessKey Secret. |","locale":"en","table":"table-18"},"3180":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-230","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#oss-oss","content":"| Parameter    | Required/Optional | Description |\n| ------------ | ----------------- | ----------- |\n| `oss.region` | Optional          | Region.     |","locale":"en","table":"table-18"},"3181":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-231","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter       | Required/Optional | Description                                                          |\n| --------------- | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hdfs.namenode` | Optional          | NameNode address; if omitted, inferred from the mount URI authority. |","locale":"en","table":"table-19"},"3182":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-232","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter   | Required/Optional | Description                                              |\n| ----------- | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hdfs.root` | Optional          | Root path; if omitted, inferred from the mount URI path. |","locale":"en","table":"table-19"},"3183":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-233","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter   | Required/Optional | Description    |\n| ----------- | ----------------- | -------------- |\n| `hdfs.user` | Optional          | HDFS username. |","locale":"en","table":"table-19"},"3184":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-234","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter               | Required/Optional | Description                             |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `hdfs.atomic_write_dir` | Optional          | Enable atomic write directory behavior. |","locale":"en","table":"table-19"},"3185":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-235","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter              | Required/Optional | Description                                                      |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hdfs.kerberos.ccache` | Optional          | Kerberos credential cache path; can also come from `KRB5CCNAME`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-19"},"3186":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-236","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter                 | Required/Optional | Description       |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------- | ----------------- |\n| `hdfs.kerberos.krb5_conf` | Optional          | `krb5.conf` path. |","locale":"en","table":"table-19"},"3187":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-237","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#hdfs-hdfs","content":"| Parameter              | Required/Optional | Description  |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------- | ------------ |\n| `hdfs.kerberos.keytab` | Optional          | Keytab path. |","locale":"en","table":"table-19"},"3188":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-238","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#webhdfs-webhdfs","content":"| Parameter          | Required/Optional | Description                                                         |\n| ------------------ | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `webhdfs.endpoint` | Optional          | WebHDFS HTTP endpoint; if omitted, inferred from the URI authority. |","locale":"en","table":"table-20"},"3189":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-239","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#webhdfs-webhdfs","content":"| Parameter      | Required/Optional | Description |\n| -------------- | ----------------- | ----------- |\n| `webhdfs.root` | Optional          | Root path.  |","locale":"en","table":"table-20"},"3190":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-240","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#webhdfs-webhdfs","content":"| Parameter            | Required/Optional | Description       |\n| -------------------- | ----------------- | ----------------- |\n| `webhdfs.delegation` | Optional          | Delegation token. |","locale":"en","table":"table-20"},"3191":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations","type":"page","content":"Operations","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals","Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations","locale":"en"},"3192":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"page","content":"Monitoring Metrics","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals","Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","locale":"en"},"3193":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-0","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#metrics-collection","content":"Metrics Collection","locale":"en"},"3194":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-1","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#master-metrics","content":"Master Metrics","locale":"en"},"3195":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-2","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#compatibility-metrics","content":"Compatibility Metrics","locale":"en"},"3196":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-3","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#journal-node-metrics","content":"Journal Node Metrics","locale":"en"},"3197":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-4","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#client-metrics","content":"Client Metrics","locale":"en"},"3198":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-5","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#worker-metrics","content":"Worker Metrics","locale":"en"},"3199":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-6","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","content":"This chapter describes the observable monitoring metrics of Curvine, used for monitoring cluster status, performance, and resource usage.","locale":"en"},"3200":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-7","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#metrics-collection","content":"Master, Worker, FUSE, the web console, and the optional Transfer service expose monitoring metrics through their HTTP ports. These metrics can be collected by Prometheus and visualized through Grafana or the built-in dashboards of `curvine-web`.","locale":"en"},"3201":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-8","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#metrics-collection","content":"Master metrics: `http://<master-host>:9010/metrics`","locale":"en"},"3202":{"id