     |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| rpc_queue_duration | Time a request waited in the RPC queue |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3219":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-26","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#master-metrics","content":"| Metric Name                | Description                              |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| replication_staging_number | Number of blocks waiting for replication |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3220":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-27","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#master-metrics","content":"| Metric Name                 | Description                                 |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| replication_inflight_number | Number of blocks currently being replicated |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3221":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-28","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#master-metrics","content":"| Metric Name               | Description                           |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| replication_failure_count | Total cumulative replication failures |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3222":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-29","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#master-metrics","content":"| Metric Name        | Description                                                   |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| operation_duration | Operation duration (classified by type, excluding heartbeats) |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3223":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-30","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#master-metrics","content":"Every service also exposes the standard Prometheus process collector on Linux\n(`process_resident_memory_bytes`, `process_cpu_seconds_total`,\n`process_open_fds`, `process_threads`). Use those for memory and CPU alerting;\nthe old `used_memory_bytes` and `rocksdb_used_memory_bytes` gauges no longer\nexist.","locale":"en"},"3224":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-31","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#compatibility-metrics","content":"The master evaluates every worker heartbeat and client handshake against its\ncompatibility contract and exposes the results as metrics (see\nVersion Management and Compatibility):","locale":"en"},"3225":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-32","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#compatibility-metrics","content":"| Metric Name           | Type  | Labels                 | Description                                            |\n| --------------------- | ----- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| compat_worker_verdict | Gauge | `worker_id`, `verdict` | 1 for the current compatibility verdict of each worker |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3226":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-33","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#compatibility-metrics","content":"| Metric Name           | Type  | Labels                   | Description                                            |\n| --------------------- | ----- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| compat_client_verdict | Gauge | `client_addr`, `verdict` | 1 for the current compatibility verdict of each client |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3227":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-34","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#compatibility-metrics","content":"| Metric Name                   | Type    | Labels                 | Description                                           |\n| ----------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| compat_enforce_rejected_total | Counter | `component`, `verdict` | Total number of enforce-mode compatibility rejections |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3228":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-35","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#compatibility-metrics","content":"The `verdict` label takes one of: `compatible`, `missing_info`, `blocked`,\n`protocol_mismatch`, `version_too_old`, `version_unknown`. Alert on\n`compat_worker_verdict` / `compat_client_verdict` with a non-`compatible`\nverdict to surface mixed-version clusters, and on `compat_enforce_rejected_total`\nincreases to catch upgrade conflicts early.","locale":"en"},"3229":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-36","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring#journal-node-metrics","content":"| Metric Name       | Description          |\n| ----------------- | -------------------- |\n| journal_queue_len | Journal queue length |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3230":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring-37","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Ma